;; MINMAX-FRAG-1 fixture 3 of 3: A PARAMETER NAMED `min`.
;; Here `(min a b)` calls the parameter, not the builtin, and the post is false
;; for a parameter returning b. The parameter is in neither the sort env nor the
;; renaming env, so a gate on those envs read it as the builtin and PROVED g.
;; Must never prove. Since FN-PARAM-UF-1 the call is opaque (a fresh result,
;; nothing assumed), so g is body-faithful and refuted.
(def-shell g [min: (fn [int int] -> int) a: int b: int] -> int
  (post (<= result a))
  (min a b))
